            "text": "**שָׁרְט** (Condition / Clause / Stipulation)\n\n---\n\n### **1. Core Concept & Identity**\nIn Hebrew script, **שָׁרְט** renders the phonetic and semantic equivalent of the Arabic word **شَرْط** (*Sharṭ*). It signifies a fundamental requirement, a binding agreement, a prerequisite, or a logical \"if-then\" operator that governs state and action.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Logical & Functional Parameters**\n\n```\n [ Antecedent / Cause ]  ===( שָׁרְט )===\u003e  [ Consequent / Effect ]\n```\n\n* **Operator:** `IF (Condition) THEN (Result)`\n* **Status:** Prerequisite / Non-negotiable\n* **State:** Pending evaluation until criteria are met.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Linguistic & Grammatical Equivalence**\n\n| Feature | Arabic | Hebrew Script (שָׁרְט) | English Meaning |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Root** | ش-ر-ط | ש-ר-ט | To stipulate, mark, impose |\n| **Noun** | שַׁרְט | שָׁרְט | Condition, term, clause |\n| **Plural** | שֻׁרוּט | שׁוּרוּט | Conditions, terms |\n\n---\n\n### **4. Operational Contexts**\n\n1. **Legal / Contractual (חוֹזֶה):**\n   * A specific clause or stipulation within an agreement that must be fulfilled for the contract to remain valid.\n\n2. **Logical / Programming (לֹוגִיקָה):**\n   * A boolean evaluation that dictates the control flow of a system.\n\n3. **Philosophical / Metaphysical (פִילוֹסוֹפְיָה):**\n   * The indispensable state of being necessary for an outcome to exist ($A \\implies B$).",
